The new signed-frame assertions in tests/storefront/buyer-browse-parity.spec.ts targeted the mobile
sort-sheet option (`a[data-sort="..."]`) on desktop as well as mobile. On desktop the sort sheet
is intentionally hidden by CSS (`apps/storefront/app/shop.css:192`) and the signed desktop frames
(782:3907, 782:3967, 782:4027) expose the active sort through the visible native `<select>`.
This aligns with the canonical click-sweep evidence (desktop "Sort by" exercised via `selectOption`)
and the existing product implementation in apps/storefront/components/ListControls.tsx.

Fix (this round): rewrite the desktop sort assertions to check the visible `<select name="sort">`
value, while keeping the mobile assertions on the visible sheet option. No product code change was
required because the production UI already matches the signed desktop frame.

